<p>		(In thousands except per share data/unaudited)*</p>
<p>NOTE:  Chrysalis International Corp said that in accordance with the pooling-of-interests method of accounting, the consolidated summary results have been restated to reflect the combination of DNX Corp and the BioClin Group for all periods presented.</p>
<p>Net income for fourth quarter and fiscal year 1996 included business combination costs of $3,649,000, or $0.32 per share, for costs incurred as a result of its acquisition of the clinical drug development business.</p>
<p>Net income for fiscal year 1995 net income included a gain of $14,566,000, or $1.24 per share, for the sale of the company's interest in Nextran.</p>
